\title{Linear independence of functions}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2021-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{A set of #{N} functions #{\lbrace f_i(x)\rbrace } is \em{linearly dependent} if}

##{\sum_{i=1}^N c_if_i(x) = 0}

\p{for #{N} constants #{c_i}, not all of which are zero. Otherwise, the functions are \em{linearly independent}. [Equivalently, if any function can be written as a linear combination of the others, they are linearly dependent.]}
